\begin_layout Subsection
Explainable genetic programming framework
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
A core feature of approaching a RL-approach with genetic programming is
 to find a measurement for how 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

complex
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 changes to his program code is for the developer to relate to.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
An easy approach is to just count the amount of operations or the amount
 of operations needed to get from the original code to the improved one.
 Even though for a computer, it might not be of great difference, for a
 human brain the type of operation is much more important.
 Adding several small values can be identified as minor adjustments to variables
 where 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

if-then-else
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 operations fundamentally change the code.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Finding the optimal weight for the adjustments is not part of this paper,
